WEBVTT

00:05.080 --> 00:08.210
Wait, your dad's been dead for years?

00:08.210 --> 00:11.580
Yeah. I heard her loud and clear.

00:12.330 --> 00:17.290
She said it when she was on
the phone with his mom.

00:18.250 --> 00:21.460
And you're sure she was
talking about your dad?!

00:21.460 --> 00:22.580
Senpai...

00:22.580 --> 00:23.790
You're sure you're not taking
something out of context?!

00:24.880 --> 00:28.460
She didn't say my dad's name...

00:28.790 --> 00:33.500
But she was talking to his mom.
Who else would they be talking about?

00:34.210 --> 00:37.250
And the way she said "it doesn't matter"...

00:37.250 --> 00:40.040
like she really doesn't
care about him anymore.

00:40.500 --> 00:44.040
Like she doesn't want anything to do with him at all.

00:44.750 --> 00:48.080
And why didn't she tell me he's gone?

00:48.830 --> 00:51.250
I love my dad.

00:51.250 --> 00:55.920
Hearing how much she hates him just,
like, broke me.

00:56.420 --> 01:00.250
I was too scared to even say anything.

02:39.040 --> 02:44.000
<b>Destiny</b>

02:48.540 --> 02:49.880
Aria-chan...

02:53.960 --> 02:55.170
Ririsa...

02:56.790 --> 03:01.330
Mayura-sama taught me this might help you feel better.

03:02.790 --> 03:04.210
Nono-pi...

03:05.630 --> 03:07.710
<b>GLANCE</b>

03:14.880 --> 03:16.040
Mikarin!

03:20.790 --> 03:21.830
You coming?

03:21.830 --> 03:23.000
I'll pass!

03:24.040 --> 03:25.250
But...

03:27.250 --> 03:29.000
My heart's with you.

03:34.380 --> 03:37.250
Thanks, everyone.

03:44.880 --> 03:49.000
C'mon, we're doing detail work today, right?
Up and at 'em, girls!

03:49.000 --> 03:50.210
Wait, but...

03:50.460 --> 03:55.920
We can't abandon our cosplays now!
Not when I'm finding out how fun this is!

03:56.500 --> 04:00.830
Besides, the most important thing
is showing him how much I love him.

04:01.580 --> 04:03.880
That's why people visit their family's graves, right?

04:03.880 --> 04:06.130
I think it depends on the person...

04:06.130 --> 04:09.040
Plus, if Okumura died on us...

04:09.040 --> 04:10.130
Wait, what?!

04:10.130 --> 04:13.790
I bet Liliel would be waiting for
him at the gates of heaven.

04:14.830 --> 04:17.420
My dad loved his manga.

04:17.420 --> 04:19.710
I'm sure Melia is there waiting to open the gates for him.

04:21.960 --> 04:23.790
C'mon, Ririsa, let's get started!

04:23.790 --> 04:24.710
O-okay!

04:24.710 --> 04:26.880
Wait, let me try on the skirt first.

04:26.880 --> 04:28.080
Okay, I'll step out!

04:32.960 --> 04:35.420
Aria's tougher than I thought.

04:36.080 --> 04:38.500
Maybe she's pretending she's okay,

04:38.500 --> 04:41.080
but the fact that she can
just shows how tough she is.

04:41.380 --> 04:45.000
But, something just doesn't feel right...

04:45.500 --> 04:48.880
The same something
I felt when started talking about VB.

04:45.500 --> 04:52.540
<b>Valykrie Battle</b>

04:48.880 --> 04:52.790
I'm not sure what, though...

04:53.880 --> 04:58.500
But, something's telling me that Kisaki-sensei isn't dead.

05:00.040 --> 05:02.880
I'm gonna have to do some research.

05:11.790 --> 05:14.000
Wow, what a feast!

05:14.330 --> 05:15.920
What inspired you today?

05:15.920 --> 05:18.830
I was lost in thought and ended
up making way too much.

05:19.250 --> 05:21.500
Aww, thanks, Aria.

05:21.500 --> 05:26.330
I'm gonna be swamped with orders for
Obon season starting tomorrow.

05:27.630 --> 05:28.670
Hey, Mom?

05:28.670 --> 05:30.790
What? I'm right here.

05:30.790 --> 05:34.250
Do you think marrying Dad was a mistake?

05:34.250 --> 05:36.580
Huh? Where's this coming from?

05:36.580 --> 05:40.000
Do you think you should've
married a rich guy instead?

05:40.000 --> 05:45.250
I don't mind not having money,
so long as I can live a happy life.

05:48.380 --> 05:51.540
Wait, do you think I divorced
him because he had no money?!

05:53.330 --> 05:57.750
I divorced him because he lost sight of his dream.

05:57.750 --> 05:58.830
Really?

05:59.750 --> 06:01.710
I'm partially to blame, too.

06:02.830 --> 06:07.960
I turned his passion into a tool to bring
in money and support our family.

06:08.250 --> 06:15.420
We were unhappy, and I knew if I stayed with him,
I'd only make him less happy.

06:15.420 --> 06:18.330
So I did what was best for both of us.

06:19.210 --> 06:21.330
So you don't hate him?

06:21.330 --> 06:23.040
Your father was a good man.

06:23.040 --> 06:25.830
He just wasn't the right
person for me or our family.

06:27.130 --> 06:28.830
Look, Aria.

06:29.420 --> 06:33.750
Life is a long series of one event after another.

06:33.750 --> 06:38.460
You can look back on them and call those
events successes or mistakes if you want.

06:38.750 --> 06:42.790
But you can't change how you
felt at the time they happened.

06:42.790 --> 06:47.080
You don't have to say you hate someone
just because you broke up with them.

06:47.790 --> 06:51.670
I was happy then, and happy now.

06:51.670 --> 06:58.040
Back then, I loved him with my whole heart.
That fact will never change.

06:58.580 --> 06:59.670
Mom...

07:00.250 --> 07:02.540
Life is about finding happiness.

07:02.540 --> 07:06.170
Don't waste it on a man
who won't give that to you.

07:08.330 --> 07:09.330
Okay.

07:14.080 --> 07:16.790
Morning, babes!

07:17.830 --> 07:18.960
Aria-chan!

07:19.250 --> 07:21.000
I'm glad you're doing better!

07:21.000 --> 07:23.000
I'm like, better than better.

07:23.000 --> 07:25.420
Wait, what's with the tension over there?

07:25.420 --> 07:28.170
Senpai's been like this all day.

07:28.170 --> 07:30.380
I think he's trying to find something online?

07:34.080 --> 07:36.000
What'd you find, Senpai?!

07:36.540 --> 07:39.790
I felt like something was off yesterday...

07:39.790 --> 07:44.380
So I started doing some research on Aria's dad.

07:45.000 --> 07:45.750
Huh?!

07:47.210 --> 07:48.420
Check this out.

07:48.750 --> 07:52.960
I found a bonus manga that wasn't
published in any of the VB volumes.

07:52.960 --> 07:55.580
Whoa, I can't believe you dug this up!

07:56.080 --> 07:57.460
Look at this!

07:59.250 --> 08:03.380
"Our esteemed master" is what
Takamatsu-sensei's assistants all called him!

08:03.710 --> 08:06.630
No one else online seems to have noticed,
but I'm pretty sure of it...

08:06.630 --> 08:10.670
Kisaki-sensei was an apprentice to the author
of the Ashford Chronicles, Takamatsu-sensei!

08:11.040 --> 08:14.420
The guy who created Liliel? I had no idea...

08:14.420 --> 08:16.960
Dad never talked about his work at home.

08:16.960 --> 08:19.170
Even if he did,
I was too little to remember.

08:19.210 --> 08:28.170
<b>Valykrie Battle</b>

08:19.500 --> 08:24.210
That's probably why people said
VB was similar to Ashford Chronicles.

08:24.210 --> 08:27.630
And probably why the Liliel
anime felt so familiar to me, too.

08:28.210 --> 08:30.580
So, what does this all mean?

08:30.580 --> 08:35.540
It'll all make sense when you
see this next thing I discovered!

08:37.670 --> 08:38.880
Look at this right here!

08:40.960 --> 08:42.290
That's Melia!

08:42.290 --> 08:44.830
No, look closer!

08:44.830 --> 08:46.380
At her ear?

08:46.380 --> 08:49.880
Every manga artist has their own way of drawing ears.

08:49.880 --> 08:54.420
Even if their art style changes,
their ear design usually stays the same.

08:55.670 --> 08:57.830
You can always tell by the ears.

08:57.830 --> 09:00.080
Senpai, why are you bringing this up?

09:00.500 --> 09:02.330
Ririsa, look closely.

09:03.380 --> 09:04.710
Do you recognize that ear?

09:06.380 --> 09:08.540
Wait, no way...

09:08.540 --> 09:11.670
Okay, why are you freaking out?!

09:12.750 --> 09:13.670
Aria...

09:15.250 --> 09:17.380
Your dad isn't dead.

09:18.500 --> 09:19.290
...what?

09:20.420 --> 09:23.210
F-for real?! How do you know?!

09:23.210 --> 09:24.000
And hold up...

09:24.830 --> 09:27.040
Why is Okumura crying?!

09:27.420 --> 09:34.130
If Kisaki-sensei had died years ago,
then none of this would be here...

09:37.250 --> 09:42.380
I think after his divorce,
he couldn't get a new series picked up...

09:42.380 --> 09:46.290
...so, because his art style was similar,
he found work with his old master.

09:46.290 --> 09:47.460
Wait...

09:48.290 --> 09:51.710
He changed his pen name and kept making manga.

09:52.250 --> 09:54.790
A spinoff of his former master's manga.

09:56.330 --> 09:57.630
Aria...

09:58.920 --> 10:00.630
I think your dad...

10:02.790 --> 10:04.500
...wrote our bible,

10:05.420 --> 10:07.540
Liliel: Side Story!

10:09.580 --> 10:11.670
How's it going, Sensei?

10:12.130 --> 10:13.330
Sensei?

10:13.830 --> 10:14.790
Kisaki-san!

10:16.880 --> 10:20.500
Sorry, I thought you'd be out today.

10:20.500 --> 10:23.040
Classical music?

10:23.040 --> 10:25.080
So that's what you're always
listening to on your headphones.

10:25.290 --> 10:29.630
Osamu Tezuka-sensei said to listen
to the highest form of music, so...

10:29.630 --> 10:33.330
I think that advice was just for newbies getting started...

10:33.330 --> 10:35.420
I mean, I did it too, way back when.

10:35.420 --> 10:38.330
Also, you got some fan mail.

10:38.580 --> 10:42.960
Thanks, but could you pass that
along to Takamatsu-sensei?

10:43.250 --> 10:47.630
You don't want to read it?
They're all from fans of Side Story.

10:48.130 --> 10:52.380
Liliel belongs to my esteemed...
Er, Takamatsu-sensei.

10:52.380 --> 10:54.960
I just write the spinoff.

10:55.670 --> 10:59.830
The only fan mail I ever got
was one letter ten years ago.

10:59.830 --> 11:03.210
C'mon, don't let it go to waste.

11:03.210 --> 11:05.500
I'm still waiting for my big debut,

11:05.500 --> 11:08.210
and if I knew I had a single fan,
I'd be over the moon.

11:09.040 --> 11:11.040
And you're sure about that?

11:11.040 --> 11:11.880
Huh?

11:12.250 --> 11:17.790
If a million readers raked your work over the coals,
would you be happy to have a single fan?

11:18.790 --> 11:20.920
Mita-kun, the reason you want to publish in Jump...

11:20.920 --> 11:23.710
..is so you can have a million
readers fall in love with your work, right?

11:23.710 --> 11:25.210
True...

11:25.210 --> 11:28.130
All these failed pitches might be getting to me.

11:28.540 --> 11:30.420
Maybe I wouldn't be happy if that happened.

11:30.580 --> 11:33.250
No, you'd be over the moon.

11:33.250 --> 11:34.210
You tricked me!

11:34.750 --> 11:36.790
I was happy to have a fan, too.

11:36.790 --> 11:40.880
I felt that, even if those million readers hated it,

11:40.880 --> 11:44.790
if one person liked it,
then it was worth making.

11:45.210 --> 11:47.080
You still have it?

11:47.080 --> 11:50.330
I wish I hadn't sent him such a disappointing response.

11:50.790 --> 11:54.170
I was so worried he would
suffer for liking my manga.

11:54.170 --> 11:58.830
Everyone was saying it was a garbage rip-off.

11:58.830 --> 12:01.210
They'd even attack people
who said they read the manga.

12:01.210 --> 12:03.420
I didn't want him to get
bullied for liking my manga.

12:03.420 --> 12:04.880
It was all too possible.

12:05.630 --> 12:11.460
But he loved my manga.
I wish I'd told him how much it meant to me.

12:11.960 --> 12:17.880
At the time, I truly believed
I deserved to disappear into obscurity.

12:18.540 --> 12:23.920
Working on the final chapters
of a canceled manga

12:23.920 --> 12:27.790
is a hell I hope you never
have to experience, Mita-kun.

12:27.790 --> 12:33.670
It's already tough enough putting
out one chapter a week.

12:34.210 --> 12:44.380
But now, you have to write a thrilling climax for
a manga no one really cares about anymore.

12:44.920 --> 12:53.750
It's like being a comedian who has to finish his set,
even though no one's laughing.

12:54.330 --> 12:58.540
You're sweaty and nauseous,
but you have to stay up on stage.

12:58.540 --> 13:02.500
Soon enough, you start believing them,
but you can't stop making the trash they hate.

13:02.500 --> 13:05.170
You start to hate your work, to hate yourself.

13:05.170 --> 13:11.040
Every day, every minute that ticks closer
to your deadline feels like an eternity.

13:14.540 --> 13:18.380
There were so many times I thought about
turning in something rushed and half-assed.

13:18.710 --> 13:23.920
But still, there was a boy out there
who thought my manga was good.

13:24.710 --> 13:30.040
Though my work would be read by a million readers,
I wrote those hundred pages for one boy.

13:30.420 --> 13:35.920
Even now, people only remember the
series for being forgettable garbage.

13:36.670 --> 13:43.880
But because I didn't throw in the towel,
now I get to keep working as a manga artist.

13:44.250 --> 13:46.920
All thanks to one fan.

13:46.920 --> 13:49.710
Oh, actually, two fans.

13:50.630 --> 13:53.130
My daughter loved my manga.

13:53.130 --> 13:55.290
I was so obsessed with work back then,

13:55.290 --> 13:58.420
I forgot to give her the love
and attention she deserved...

13:59.000 --> 14:01.040
He was the same age as my daughter.

14:01.710 --> 14:03.630
<b>Manga Club</b>

14:01.960 --> 14:07.000
I hope both of them still love manga now.

14:16.080 --> 14:18.000
<b>Manga Club</b>

14:18.040 --> 14:20.420
Liliel!

14:20.920 --> 14:21.710
Huh?

14:22.080 --> 14:22.920
Iconic Senpai.

14:22.920 --> 14:23.830
Hello.

14:23.830 --> 14:24.830
Hey, babe!

14:25.040 --> 14:26.210
Okumura?

14:26.210 --> 14:30.000
I went back to the anime to
check stuff and got distracted.

14:30.000 --> 14:33.580
Did you ask your mom about that phone call, Aria?

14:33.580 --> 14:36.750
Yeah. I asked her about it yesterday, and, uh...

14:37.790 --> 14:40.210
You mean that call with your grandmother?

14:41.630 --> 14:45.000
She called about one of his
relatives that passed a while back.

14:45.290 --> 14:48.170
What?! Why was she calling you about that?!

14:48.170 --> 14:51.630
God, it's so stupid.
I lent him 100K yen a long time ago.

14:51.630 --> 14:54.670
We hit it off at a family funeral,
and I was happy to help.

14:54.670 --> 14:56.460
You hit it off at a funeral?

14:56.460 --> 14:59.920
Anyway, he told me he couldn't pay me back,
so I stopped talking to him.

14:59.920 --> 15:03.540
He died five years ago.

15:03.540 --> 15:08.460
Grandma apparently found out about the
debt and wants to make sure I'm paid back.

15:08.460 --> 15:12.380
But, I honestly don't care about him or the cash,
so I told her to forget it.

15:12.630 --> 15:14.210
Were you just curious, or...

15:14.210 --> 15:17.670
N-no.... never mind.

15:19.130 --> 15:23.920
So Okumura was totally right,
I was taking it out context... My bad.

15:23.920 --> 15:24.710
It's okay!

15:24.710 --> 15:28.380
No, that's good. That all but confirms it.

15:28.830 --> 15:32.750
Kisaki-sensei has to be the author of Liliel: Side Story!

15:33.630 --> 15:35.960
I still don't fully believe it...

15:35.960 --> 15:39.790
But, you're the biggest Liliel Otaku in the world,
so I think we have to.

15:39.790 --> 15:44.960
Ever since you mentioned it,
I've noticed how similar the art and story is.

15:44.960 --> 15:45.960
This is crazy...

15:45.960 --> 15:50.330
The artist who created the first
manga I fell in love with...

15:50.330 --> 15:53.630
...has been bringing us new
Liliel content for the past ten years.

15:54.080 --> 15:55.330
Senpai...

15:56.290 --> 15:59.630
But, I shouldn't get emotional about
this until we know for sure.

15:59.630 --> 16:05.040
Okay, but if that's true,
then if our Liliel cosplays stand out...

16:05.630 --> 16:09.630
...then there's a good chance
Kisaki-sensei will hear about them!

16:13.130 --> 16:17.290
Now I'm super pumped to get this done.
Let's finish our costumes, Ririsa!

16:17.290 --> 16:21.000
Yeah! With summer break just around the corner,
we'll have tons of time!

16:21.000 --> 16:23.000
I'll help, too!

16:23.000 --> 16:24.630
Don't forget about your homework, though.

16:26.130 --> 16:27.460
Aria-chan, Aria-chan!

16:28.500 --> 16:30.210
Wait, that's so good!

16:30.880 --> 16:31.830
What's good?

16:32.040 --> 16:33.580
Nothing you need to know.

16:32.250 --> 16:33.290
<b>hehehe</b>

16:35.540 --> 16:38.790
You guys should know that
Comiket's got its upsides and downsides.

16:39.830 --> 16:42.130
Comiket's absolutely ginormous.

16:42.380 --> 16:46.210
They've got set locations and structured
lines to corral those thousands of attendees.

16:46.540 --> 16:51.790
Photo time is extremely limited,
and tons of famous cosplayers will be there, too.

16:51.790 --> 16:53.960
That includes all four of the Heavenly Queens.

16:54.210 --> 16:57.250
B-but hey, Liliel and Nono-pi are ranked
fifth and fourth on the Rising Stars list!

16:57.250 --> 17:00.290
First through third will be there, too.

17:01.080 --> 17:03.540
Mr. Camera said he'd announced
who they were before Comiket.

17:03.960 --> 17:08.130
And our photos will be drowned out by
the ocean of Comiket pics posted online.

17:08.130 --> 17:12.040
It's actually harder to go viral from
Comiket than other events.

17:12.460 --> 17:14.290
Especially, Summer Comiket.

17:14.290 --> 17:16.420
It's practically haunted.

17:16.670 --> 17:17.630
Haunted?

17:17.630 --> 17:19.420
We should aim for Day 3,

17:19.420 --> 17:22.290
since that's when cosplayers
will be selling their ROMs.

17:22.540 --> 17:25.580
Nagomi might stay, but Erica and Yoki might not.

17:25.580 --> 17:30.710
Okay! And this year's Comiket
is August 8th through 11th, so...

17:30.960 --> 17:34.000
Oh, I can't. My mom and I leave on the
10th to visit our family grave for Obon.

17:34.000 --> 17:35.000
You're so normal!

17:35.000 --> 17:35.790
That's so nice of you!

17:35.790 --> 17:37.580
You two know you're going to hell, right?

17:37.880 --> 17:41.250
All that's left, then, is to make your announcement.

17:41.250 --> 17:44.080
Most people decide who they want
to see the day before they go,

17:44.080 --> 17:45.420
so posting about it is critical.

17:45.830 --> 17:51.210
I-I posted about it,
but I didn't get as many shares as Nagomi-san...

17:54.040 --> 17:58.040
Okay, fine.
I guess I can make some kind of announcement.

17:58.040 --> 17:59.790
You're the best, Mikari-chan!

17:59.790 --> 18:02.250
If Mikarin makes a post on her socials, we're golden...

18:02.250 --> 18:03.290
Please.

18:04.040 --> 18:09.000
If our competition is posting online,
I'm not about to stoop to their level.

18:12.170 --> 18:17.210
I'm gonna be at Comiket on Day 1
with a Liliel Defense Squadron group!

18:17.210 --> 18:22.040
Whoa, hold on, you serious?!
You're gonna be cosplaying?!

18:22.040 --> 18:24.830
Yeah! I even made my costume!

18:24.830 --> 18:26.540
You announced it on TV...

18:26.540 --> 18:27.960
Well? Didn't I do good?

18:28.920 --> 18:31.000
Sensei, you're not gonna believe this!

18:32.460 --> 18:37.080
Mikarin is going to Comiket in a Liliel cosplay!
You lucky dog, you!

18:37.540 --> 18:38.500
Who?

18:38.500 --> 18:39.540
Seriously?

18:39.880 --> 18:43.920
You know that cute Liliel cosplayer that
went around social media recently?

18:43.920 --> 18:47.080
Yeah, I heard something about that.

18:47.080 --> 18:50.750
She's gonna be cosplaying with her!
We've gotta go see them in person!

18:50.750 --> 18:53.710
No, I'll pass. It'll be too hot and crowded.

18:53.710 --> 18:56.710
What, and give up the opportunity to
see your characters cosplayed?!

18:56.710 --> 18:58.250
You've gotta want to see them in person!

18:58.250 --> 19:01.330
Cosplayers are getting
crazy good these days, too!

19:01.540 --> 19:04.330
I'd want to if it were my own series.

19:04.330 --> 19:06.080
Not this again.

19:06.080 --> 19:10.210
They're doing the Airborne Defense Squadron!
That's Side Story!

19:10.750 --> 19:15.290
And Ariel isn't in the original! She's your character!

19:17.460 --> 19:20.000
Don't you want to see Ariel in person?

19:25.790 --> 19:26.960
Did I upset him?

19:29.080 --> 19:35.130
Oh! I know this song, Sensei!
It's the one where the violin and G?

19:35.130 --> 19:36.960
Johann Sebastian Bach,

19:36.960 --> 19:42.920
Orchestral Suite No. 3 in D Major,
second movement, Air on the G String.

19:44.250 --> 19:45.630
Or, "Aria."

19:46.880 --> 19:49.710
It's my favorite piece of music in the entire world.

19:50.710 --> 19:54.580
Mita-kun, let me think it over.

19:55.500 --> 19:56.880
All right!

20:01.500 --> 20:07.670
The contours, the reflectivity,
the scaling, the overall balance...

20:13.290 --> 20:14.830
It's perfect!

20:18.500 --> 20:21.040
We passed Okumura's final check!

20:21.040 --> 20:22.790
So that means...

20:23.080 --> 20:25.170
Ariel is done!

20:25.170 --> 20:27.540
Thanks, everyone!

20:27.540 --> 20:29.460
Took you guys long enough.

20:31.540 --> 20:35.130
<b>Valykrie Battle</b>

20:32.000 --> 20:34.420
Just you wait, Kisaki-sensei.

20:34.790 --> 20:36.920
You don't need to protect me.

20:36.920 --> 20:41.420
I'll tell everyone how much I love your
series a thousand times if I have to.

20:43.040 --> 20:45.130
Because that's what otaku do!

20:49.040 --> 20:51.790
I always get so excited the morning of.

20:51.790 --> 20:52.790
Same!

20:52.790 --> 20:54.250
Ririsa-chan!

20:54.960 --> 20:56.290
Morning, babes!

20:56.290 --> 20:57.210
Morning!

20:57.210 --> 20:58.630
Senpai!

20:58.630 --> 21:01.000
Okay, we're all here.

21:02.790 --> 21:06.710
We should get to Kokusai-Tenjijo station before 8.

21:07.040 --> 21:09.630
It's nice getting to relax.
Usually, I'm on the first train here.

21:09.630 --> 21:11.540
Wait, at like 4 AM?!

21:11.540 --> 21:13.080
You guys are nuts.

21:13.920 --> 21:16.920
Everyone feeling good?
It's gonna get hot today.

21:17.170 --> 21:19.500
I had a hard time getting to sleep 'cause I was so excited.

21:19.500 --> 21:20.960
I'm full of energy!

21:22.380 --> 21:24.790
Remember everything today, Ririsa?

21:24.790 --> 21:27.210
I-I've got everything!

21:27.500 --> 21:31.500
Hey, you made that mistake once,
now you'll never make it again!

21:31.500 --> 21:36.790
I slept well, ate breakfast,
remembered everything, and am ready to go!

21:37.040 --> 21:40.880
I've got zero anxiety this morning!

21:40.880 --> 21:41.920
You just jinxed it!

21:44.080 --> 21:46.460
They must all be cosplayers. They've all got bags.

21:46.460 --> 21:50.290
Look at that guy and his harem. Lucky bastard.

21:50.290 --> 21:52.710
Harem? You've got it wrong.

21:54.130 --> 21:57.750
Those are the eyes of a man
who only gets aroused by 2D girls!

21:58.290 --> 21:59.880
Forgive me, comrade.

21:59.880 --> 22:00.790
Comrade.

22:00.790 --> 22:01.830
Hello, comrades.

22:19.960 --> 22:21.710
Let's go! It's time...

22:22.380 --> 22:23.670
...for Comiket!

23:56.130 --> 24:01.130
<b>Time for Summer Comiket!</b>
